# gadak agent demo — one line of setup, then a real Claude Code session that
# answers a question no JQL query can express, using the local mirror.
#
# Regenerated by `make media-agent`, which requires BOTH:
#   bash tools/tapes/prepare.sh          (mirror + binary)
#   bash tools/tapes/prepare-agent.sh    (isolated HOME with Claude Code auth)
# Run `bash tools/tapes/prepare-agent.sh --clean` afterwards — it holds a copy
# of this machine's Claude credentials.
#
# Nothing here is scripted output: the second scene really calls the model,
# which really calls gadak's MCP tools. Takes vary, so re-run until one reads
# well. Everything visible comes from the demo mirror (examples/demo.db).
#
# Sizing mirrors tui.tape: 77 cols × 24 rows, big glyphs, because the README
# renders this at 800 px. See the sizing note in tui.tape before changing it.
#
# Size: the committed asset is this tape's output run through
# `gifsicle -O3 --colors 64` (see docs/MEDIA.md).

Output docs/media/agent.gif

Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 20
Set FontFamily "D2Coding, Menlo, Monaco, monospace"
Set Width 1080
Set Height 620
Set Theme "Catppuccin Mocha"
Set Padding 14
Set Framerate 8
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Set WindowBar Colorful
Set BorderRadius 6
Set WaitTimeout 120s

# Neutral shell: no user@host, no real $HOME path. HOME points at the throwaway
# agent home, so the paths Claude Code prints below carry no identity.
Hide
# `|| exit 1` is a safety interlock, not tidiness: without env-agent.sh the
# shell would keep going with the *operator's* real HOME and no GADAK_HOME, and
# the take would record a live Jira mirror. Fail the recording instead.
Type "source tools/tapes/.tmp/env-agent.sh || exit 1"
Enter
Type "clear"
Enter
Show

Sleep 500ms

# ── Setup: one line teaches any MCP client about the mirror ────────────────
Type "claude mcp add gadak -- gadak mcp"
Enter
Sleep 2.5s

Type "clear"
Enter
Sleep 400ms

# ── The session: a question that spans issues, history, and wiki pages ─────
Type "claude"
Enter
Sleep 4s

Type "Which epic has the most reopened issues? One line."
Sleep 600ms
Enter

# The model works here: tool calls to gadak_query stream in as they happen, and
# the answer lands around 15–20 s. Timing is not deterministic, so this sleep is
# sized for a slow take and the idle tail is cut in the gifsicle pass (the frame
# range is picked per take — see docs/MEDIA.md).
Sleep 25s

# Leave the session.
Ctrl+C
Sleep 400ms
Ctrl+C
Sleep 800ms
